event.review:
The draft covers setup of prerequisite user profile, membership, and post. Each invalid attachment upload is tested for a specific schema or domain error: missing required fields, invalid file_size, and invalid mime_type. Each expects error by using TestValidator.error.

However, TypeScript type safety is crucial, and omitting required fields or setting invalid primitive types (such as negative file_size, if file_size is unsigned or string format) is not possible due to strict typing. Only non-type-level (business) errors can be tested at runtime, while compile-time errors should not be coded (per requirements). So, the test for missing required fields (step 4) involving incomplete payloads must be omitted. Instead, only payloads that are valid TypeScript but invalid per the business/domain (file_size < 0, empty mime_type) can be tested.

@ts-expect-error or as any must not be used in production code. Only schema-valid (TypeScript-valid) but business-invalid properties are allowed in error tests.

